index 0000000..6692774
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/dicode-codex-mvp.md
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# DiCode Codex MVP deployment
+
+The standalone `dicode-codex-bridge` receives `POST /codex/v1/responses`. It checks the caller's DiCode bearer token and selected model through the existing `model-proxy` model-access service. It calls the already Responses-compatible gateway using a separate API key from Kubernetes Secret `dicode-codex-gateway`, sends `originator: codex_cli_rs` plus session/thread IDs, and streams the original Responses events. The VS Code extension starts an unmodified local Codex CLI; no Codex process runs in the Kubernetes container.
+
+## Offline artifacts
+
+The release contains `dicode-codex-bridge-v0.1.1-linux-amd64-image.tar`, `dicode-codex-cli-0.164.0-assets.tar`, `dicode-codex-mvp.vsix`, the deployment patch, and a SHA-256 file. Copy them into one directory on the internal network and run `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS-dicode-codex-mvp-v0.1.2.txt`. The bridge image is for **linux/amd64** cluster nodes. The CLI asset archive contains the official Codex 0.164.0 **Linux and Windows x64/arm64** platform packages.
+
+## Install the new service only
+
+1. On a machine with Docker and access to your internal registry, run:
+
+   ```sh
+   docker load -i dicode-codex-bridge-v0.1.1-linux-amd64-image.tar
+   docker tag costrict/dicode-codex-bridge:v0.1.1 REGISTRY/PROJECT/dicode-codex-bridge:v0.1.1
+   docker push REGISTRY/PROJECT/dicode-codex-bridge:v0.1.1
+   ```
+
+2. Create the gateway-key Secret in the target cluster from a local file containing only the key (for example, the key used to call the gateway directly). Do not put this key in `configure.sh` or the VSIX:
+
+   ```sh
+   kubectl -n costrict create secret generic dicode-codex-gateway \
+     --from-file=api-key=/secure/path/gateway-key.txt \
+     --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
+   ```
+
+3. In this deployment repository, set `IMAGE_DICODE_CODEX_BRIDGE` in `scripts/newest-images.list` to `REGISTRY/PROJECT/dicode-codex-bridge:v0.1.1`. Set `CODEX_GATEWAY_RESPONSES_URL` in `configure.sh` to `https://yice.byd.com/ai-gate/v1/responses`, or the corresponding internal address. The bridge must be able to reach that URL from the cluster. The caller's DiCode JWT is used only for model-access authorization; the Secret key is used only for the gateway.
+4. Run `./costrict.sh prepare`. Check the generated `k8s/dicode-codex-bridge.yaml`, then apply only this new service:
+
+   ```sh
+   kubectl apply -f k8s/dicode-codex-bridge.yaml
+   kubectl -n costrict rollout status deployment/dicode-codex-bridge
+   ```
+
+5. Set the APISIX route. In one terminal run `kubectl -n costrict port-forward svc/apisix 39180:9180`. In another terminal, from this repository:
+
+   ```sh
+   source ./configure.sh
+   export APISIX_ADDR AUTH TYPE
+   ./scripts/apisix_router/dicode-codex-bridge.sh
+   ```
+
+   The public route is `POST /codex/v1/responses`. You can also use the existing `./apisix_router_setting.sh` workflow, which reapplies all routes.
+
+For a direct check, `kubectl -n costrict port-forward svc/dicode-codex-bridge 18080:8080`, then send a Responses request to `http://127.0.0.1:18080/codex/v1/responses` using a **DiCode user bearer token** and a model visible in `/ai-gateway/api/v1/models`. Do not send the gateway API key to the bridge as the user token. Check `kubectl -n costrict logs deployment/dicode-codex-bridge` if the model check or gateway call fails.
+
+## Codex CLI auto-install assets
+
+With a running `portal` deployment, execute `./scripts/deploy-dicode-codex-cli-assets.sh /path/to/dicode-codex-cli-0.164.0-assets.tar`. This places the platform manifests and archives under `/var/www/costrict/codex/` on the existing portal volume. Verify from a workstation that `<APISIX_BASE_URL>/costrict/codex/linux/x64/manifest.json` and `<APISIX_BASE_URL>/costrict/codex/win32/x64/manifest.json` return JSON. The VSIX downloads the matching archive on first activation, checks its SHA-256, and installs it in the extension host's private storage. For later CLI releases, create a new asset archive using `node scripts/package-dicode-codex-cli.js VERSION LINUX_X64_TGZ WINDOWS_X64_TGZ LINUX_ARM64_TGZ WINDOWS_ARM64_TGZ OUTPUT_TAR` from the main repository, then redeploy these static assets.
+
+## Workstation
+
+Install the separate `dicode-codex-mvp.vsix` on the workstation or remote extension host. The VSIX automatically downloads and installs Codex CLI on first activation when `dicodeCodex.codexPath` is left at its default `codex`. Set `dicodeCodex.serverUrl` to the APISIX entry URL if the default is not your internal address. An explicit `dicodeCodex.codexPath` overrides automatic installation. On Windows, the extension host downloads the Windows package; on WSL or remote Linux, it downloads the Linux package.
+
+The bridge's `/health` endpoint is only for Kubernetes probes. Model authorization is checked on every Responses request. Existing login, model list, and Chat-RAG routes remain on their current services.
diff --git a/k8s/dicode-codex-bridge.yaml.tpl b/k8s/dicode-codex-bridge.yaml.tpl
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f7bef3c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/k8s/dicode-codex-bridge.yaml.tpl
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+apiVersion: v1
+kind: Service
+metadata:
+  name: dicode-codex-bridge
+  namespace: {{K8S_NAMESPACE}}
+spec:
+  selector:
+    app: dicode-codex-bridge
+  ports:
+    - name: http
+      port: 8080
+      targetPort: 8080
+---
+apiVersion: apps/v1
+kind: Deployment
+metadata:
+  name: dicode-codex-bridge
+  namespace: {{K8S_NAMESPACE}}
+spec:
+  replicas: 1
+  selector:
+    matchLabels:
+      app: dicode-codex-bridge
+  template:
+    metadata:
+      labels:
+        app: dicode-codex-bridge
+    spec:
+      nodeSelector:
+        {{K8S_NODE_SELECTOR_KEY}}: "{{K8S_NODE_SELECTOR_VALUE}}"
+      containers:
+        - name: bridge
+          image: {{IMAGE_DICODE_CODEX_BRIDGE}}
+          imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
+          env:
+            - name: MODEL_ACCESS_URL
+              value: "http://model-proxy:8080/ai-gateway/api/v1/models"
+            - name: GATEWAY_RESPONSES_URL
+              value: "{{CODEX_GATEWAY_RESPONSES_URL}}"
+            - name: GATEWAY_API_KEY
+              valueFrom:
+                secretKeyRef:
+                  name: dicode-codex-gateway
+                  key: api-key
+          ports:
+            - name: http
+              containerPort: 8080
+          readinessProbe:
+            httpGet:
+              path: /health
+              port: http
+          livenessProbe:
+            httpGet:
+              path: /health
+              port: http
diff --git a/scripts/apisix_router/dicode-codex-bridge.sh b/scripts/apisix_router/dicode-codex-bridge.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..ee386be
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/apisix_router/dicode-codex-bridge.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+set -eu
+
+curl --fail-with-body -sS "http://$APISIX_ADDR/apisix/admin/upstreams" -H "$AUTH" -H "$TYPE" -X PUT -d '{
+  "id": "dicode-codex-bridge",
+  "nodes": { "dicode-codex-bridge:8080": 1 },
+  "type": "roundrobin"
+}'
+
+curl --fail-with-body -sS "http://$APISIX_ADDR/apisix/admin/routes" -H "$AUTH" -H "$TYPE" -X PUT -d '{
+  "id": "dicode-codex-bridge",
+  "name": "dicode-codex-responses",
+  "uris": ["/codex/v1/responses"],
+  "methods": ["POST"],
+  "upstream_id": "dicode-codex-bridge",
+  "status": 1
+}'
diff --git a/scripts/deploy-dicode-codex-cli-assets.sh b/scripts/deploy-dicode-codex-cli-assets.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..2758b1b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/deploy-dicode-codex-cli-assets.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -euo pipefail
+
+if [[ $# -ne 1 || ! -f "$1" ]]; then
+  echo "usage: $0 dicode-codex-cli-0.164.0-assets.tar" >&2
+  exit 2
+fi
+
+namespace="${K8S_NAMESPACE:-costrict}"
+destination="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/dicode-codex-assets.XXXXXXXX")"
+trap 'rm -rf -- "${destination}"' EXIT
+tar -xf "$1" -C "${destination}"
+
+pod="$(kubectl -n "${namespace}" get pod -l app=portal --field-selector=status.phase=Running -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}')"
+if [[ -z "${pod}" ]]; then
+  echo "portal pod is not running in namespace ${namespace}" >&2
+  exit 1
+fi
+kubectl -n "${namespace}" exec "${pod}" -- mkdir -p /var/www/costrict/codex
+kubectl -n "${namespace}" cp "${destination}/." "${pod}:/var/www/costrict/codex/"
+echo "Codex CLI assets deployed to portal pod ${pod}"
